0 Two short track units carry broad hinged pads around small and large gear wheels.
0 Name: TECHNIC_CHAIN_TREAD-Constraints.ldr
0 Author: Willy Tschager
0 Unofficial Model
0 // Scene: One track has a larger, taller oval envelope than the other. Transparent brick rails sit inside the loops, leaving the wheel centres and the underside of the pads visible.
0 // Rigid construction: 3702 and 3700 Technic bricks, plates and 3749 axle pins provide small carrier frames. The two examples compare 3648b 24-tooth and 3649 40-tooth wheels.
0 // Build lesson: Build a track module from its carrier rail and wheel centres outward. Track width, end-wheel size and visible pad spacing strongly determine the vehicle silhouette.
0 // Reuse: These are separate size comparisons, not a finished matched pair of vehicle tracks. Colour 16 is unresolved in one block; drive, axle retention and full chassis attachment need review.
0 ROTATION CENTER 0 0 0 1 "Custom" 
0 ROTATION CONFIG 0 0
